> So, why not just allow wishing of an altar?

Because the altar would be a way to increase early-game survivability 
for a player not having found anything sufficiently useful to allow him 
to dive deeper into the dungeon without having to fear to be killed 
anytime.  If you have a wish available, you don't need an altar.  You 
can just wish for a good weapon or a piece of armor that allows you to 
survive longer with your crappy one.

Anyway, I would not mind allowing to obtain altars by wishes.  It does 
not seem unbalanced to me.

But getting an altar and obtaining your artifact by sacrificing is much 
more stylish than just wishing for it (also it has the additional 
benefit of allowing you to get unrestricted in the weapon).

Here is how I would set up things:

You need:  an uncursed scroll of earth  (go to Sokoban)
            a means of confusing yourself (potion or burnt-out spell,
               but you must avoid being stun as well)
            a means to get hallucination (potion or appropriate fungi)
            a space of 7 by 7 squares free of any obstacle
               (including walls, stairs, traps, so search it carefully)
            a means of digging or a scroll of teleportation,
               in case something goes wrong

Get to the center of the area.  Confuse yourself and read the scroll of 
earth.  You should get the usual effects of the scroll of earth with the 
minor modification that if it is blessed or uncursed, the boulders 
around you will merge into a wall.  If it is cursed, one could create a 
trap instead of the boulder falling on you.

If the scroll was blessed or uncursed, you are now surrounded by a 
closed wall delimiting a three-by-three square.  If you wore a helmet, 
you are screwed and should dig or teleport out.  If you did not wear a 
helmet "a wave is emanating from your brain pushing back the walls", and 
each wall moves by one or two lattice units outwards, so you will get a 
rectangular room, which can be as sizable as a seven-by-seven square. 
If one of the walls hits an obstacle during motion, the ritual will be 
screwed up.  (To avoid creating an altar on certain special levels, 
every square of that level could get the "obstacle" property.)  Since 
scrolls of earth don't work on the planes, creating an altar there by 
"ritual" would be impossible.

If your scroll of earth was blessed, you are screwed, too, as you will 
need to sit on a boulder that is to become an altar.  That is, you must 
not wear a helmet to have the walls move outside (to get at least one 
free space from the altar to each wall), but not wearing a helmet will 
make you suffer some damage from the boulder falling on your head.  So 
the procedure is not advisable to a first- or second-level character or 
if you are low on Hp.

Note that the walls are closed so far, so you will have to dig out or 
teleport, if your scroll was blessed.

If your scroll was uncursed, you should be on the same square with a 
boulder now and have your temple walls.  Next you need to get yourself 
hallucinating while still confused.  Then pray.

If your prayer timeout has not passed yet, the boulder will turn into a 
trap, which might teleport you out, if it is a teleportation trap.  If 
your god is angry at you, you will get a pool or a pool of lava instead, 
the latter, if your god is severely angry.  In that case, if you don't 
have fire resistance, you will just get fried.

If your prayer timeout has passed and your god is on friendly terms with 
you, you will get an altar, but a random one, and a door will be created 
in one of the four walls to the north, east, south or west of the altar.
Your prayer timeout will be reset as if you had done a wish.

If your altar is not coaligned, your god will *now* be angry with you 
and your alignment will become negative (as if you had killed your quest 
leader, for example).  You will then not be able to use the altar for 
some time (after your prayer timeout has become zero, you might get 
unholy water from it, but I guess for that you would still have to 
appease your god first).   You should walk around doing some kills until 
you feel your alignment to be positive and then you may convert the 
altar by an appropriate sacrifice.

If the altar is coaligned, you have hit the jackpot.  Your alignment 
will get a positive boost, and you can start sacrificing right away. 
You still cannot pray for holy water, before your prayer timeout has 
been dissipated.

